The R2 training copy reproduces the originals exactly:
- seed-mean scores for voice_df and voice_ad (max diff 0) and music 6+12 (6.6e-5);
- per-seed P1 CPU results (best epochs 39/24/50, val 0.049175/0.050964/0.049175);
- DurBal val EERs;
- S3-like held-out ADS 0.87267.

evidence:
- review/v1/comp_r2.py retrains R2 exactly: max |diff| vs r2/runs 7.8e-10 (DF MLP) and 4.3e-8 (AD ResMLP).
- eval_semantics_voice_df_mlp_voice_ad_resmlp.json:
  - runtime|S3+both - runtime|S3: +0.01389, CI 0.01005-0.01736;
  - unseen: +0.0145, CI 0.00914-0.0183;
  - seen: +0.01371, CI 0.00564-0.02213;
  - unseen voice EER 0.12376 -> 0.07345.
- review/v1/r2_seen.json (screen semantics, same conclusion).
- lb_noise.json: 1,200-file draws, mean +0.0134-0.0137, SD 0.0034-0.0036, 95% range 0.0067-0.0208.
- Protocol hygiene: r2/run.py saves test_preds without scoring them; logs/*.log contain val only; choice_lock.json written 14:04:45; test scoring happens in report.py test.

counterevidence:
It survives every check I ran. Remaining risks are all outside held-out validity:
- the DB -> P1 protocol refit is untested (no held-out estimate is possible);
- the post-hoc protocol amendment at 14:02 added the DF MLP after the AD MLP val results, but it used val only;
- the S4 implementation currently deviates from the validated configuration (see required fix).

A paired ADS delta measured on a 1,200-file test is itself noisy:
- SD about 0.006 for S3-sized changes, about 0.002 for changes of about +0.0015;
- the S3 LB value +0.0153 has P = 0.13-0.18 under held-out-like draws;
- the S3 transfer ratio is 1.84 (+0.0153 / +0.0083).
Ratios computed from single +/-0.002 LB moves (P1, S2a) are noise. The seen-row gain (+0.0148 runtime) matching the LB is coincidentally consistent, not diagnostic.

The headline variant (FILE keeps S3's Fv; 0.87731) was added after the coupled variant scored 0.87605. Val also prefers it (0.93044 vs 0.93003), so selection bias is small. Two things remain open:
- its LB sign depends on the share of voice/music-discordant files in the official test (UNVERIFIED);
- it is untested on top of the R2 MLP heads, which already cut held-out voice EER to 0.0823, so the gains may overlap.
